{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/940965-mortal-cultists-of-the-dark-mother","id":940965,"title":"Mortal cultists of the Dark Mother?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T17:49:46-07:00","id":940965,"title":"Mortal cultists of the Dark Mother?","content":"Just wondering, what sorts of structures and traits would Dark Mother-worshipping cults be likely to have? It's inevitable that mortals would find out about her, and especially given how cult-prone the world of darkness is, some of them would probably start worshipping her in various ways. I'm assuming there would be a range of responses among Beasts- with some of them, of course, being willing to exploit these cultists as minions. <br /> <br /> The canonical compact The Reckoning would fit in with this. They aren't exactly &quot;fear cultists&quot;, but they are a religious group that works with Beasts. It'd be interesting seeing the kinds of theological disputes that happen when their members meet other cultists. <br /> <br /> The idea was actually inspired by Demon and the SCP Foundation- Demon has mortal and Stigmatic cultists of the God-Machine, and that made me think of the Church of the Broken God from the SCP verse, which in turn made me think of the Sarkicism vs. Mekhanism conflict, which made me think of the potential for setting up the God-Machine and the Dark Mother as opposing forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-10-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T20:05:13-07:00","id":941007,"title":"","content":"One could argue that Irem and the Nameless Empire as a whole were influenced by the Dark Mother if you interpret her as being related to Ammut. Hell, take a look at the Judges - all horrifically monstrous, all focused around shaping mankind according to their strange laws and lessons - and tell me that they aren't all very scary Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T20:44:58-07:00","id":941016,"title":"","content":"I can imagine at least one cult of Luddites who believe that humans have reached too far and need to be &quot;put in their place&quot; before they unleash something terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:05:48-07:00","id":941148,"title":"","content":"Would it be any different from most non-cult organizations? Live our way or be punished in some ethereal way after your death, and some physical or social way during your life. Depictions of the Dark Mother would be changed to something more easily accepted by the masses once you got to a certain point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:45:53-07:00","id":941260,"title":"","content":"From what's been hinted about the Dark Mother in the book, she actually loves her children. She encourages them to be both monstrous and wise. Even though Beasts have the strongest connection to Her, she may extend that love and respect to human beings who act sufficiently monstrous. People receptive to that idea may want to establish a connection in any way they can. This can involve learning and following Her teachings at great personal risk, or developing actual Supernatural Merits (Like Communion from Second Sight).<br /> <br /> There are several ways this can play out. The bigger the cult, the greater the chance it reaches the lowest common denominator, and whoever is in charge trades love and wisdom for selfish power. Things will likely go downhill afterwards. On the other hand, cooler heads might prevail and create a community that functions as well as any other, but with very different Sundays and Holidays. A smaller group, especially if its member are close to each other, may succeed in developing a non-standard ethical system. Better yet, cult members may try to pass their dogma to their children. Whether it ruins their upbringing, or creates functional but incredibly odd adults is up in the air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T17:09:24-07:00","id":941518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/940965-mortal-cultists-of-the-dark-mother?p=941260#post941260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what's been hinted about the Dark Mother in the book, she actually loves her children. She encourages them to be both monstrous and wise. Even though Beasts have the strongest connection to Her, she may extend that love and respect to human beings who act sufficiently monstrous. People receptive to that idea may want to establish a connection in any way they can. This can involve learning and following Her teachings at great personal risk, or developing actual Supernatural Merits (Like Communion from Second Sight).</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is where Slashers come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darknes